  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two billiard balls of equal mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> strike a rigid wall with same speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>108</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kmph</mi></math> (as shown) but at different angles. If the balls get reflected with the same speed, then the ratio of the magnitude of impulses imparted to ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;and ball <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;by the wall along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>&nbsp;direction is:</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e0cb0fa7-cf71-4c69-ac2f-f0cdd7551054-image.png\" style=\"width: 330px; height: 163px;\" /></p>",
